# Mercury Agent Trivy Ignore Configuration
# This file specifies vulnerabilities to ignore during Trivy scans
# Use with caution - only ignore after careful assessment
#
# Last Updated: 2026-01-06
# Reviewed By: Security Team
# Next Review: 2026-04-06 (quarterly)

# =============================================================================
# CVE-2025-14104: util-linux heap buffer overread in setpwnam()
# =============================================================================
# Severity: Medium
# Component: util-linux (libblkid1, libmount1, libsmartcols1, libuuid1)
# Description: Heap buffer overread when processing 256-byte usernames
#
# Risk Assessment:
# - CVSS Score: 5.5 (Medium)
# - Attack Vector: Local
# - Privileges Required: Low
# - User Interaction: None
#
# Justification for Acceptance:
# 1. Mercury Agent runs as non-root user (mercuryagent, UID 1000)
# 2. Application does not handle passwd/user management operations
# 3. No SUID binaries are used by the application
# 4. Container removes setuid/setgid bits from all binaries
# 5. Application does not process usernames of any length
# 6. The vulnerable function (setpwnam) is not called by application code
#
# Mitigations Applied:
# - Non-root container execution (USER mercuryagent)
# - SUID/SGID bits removed from all binaries
# - login/passwd packages purged from runtime image
# - Multi-stage build minimizes attack surface
#
# Review Date: 2026-01-06
# Expiry: 2026-04-06 (re-evaluate if upstream patch available)
CVE-2025-14104

# =============================================================================
# CVE-2025-8869: pip symlink extraction vulnerability
# =============================================================================
# Severity: Medium
# Component: pip
# Description: Missing checks on symbolic link extraction
#
# Risk Assessment:
# - CVSS Score: 5.3 (Medium)
# - Attack Vector: Network
# - Privileges Required: None
# - User Interaction: Required (user must install malicious package)
#
# Justification for Acceptance:
# 1. pip is upgraded to >=25.1 in builder stage
# 2. Python 3.12 base image implements PEP 706, so the vulnerable
#    tar fallback code path is never executed
# 3. All packages installed from PyPI with HTTPS verification
# 4. No untrusted package sources configured
# 5. Container runs as non-root user limiting symlink attack impact
# 6. Production containers do not run pip install at runtime
#
# Mitigations Applied:
# - pip upgraded to latest version (>=25.1)
# - Python 3.12 PEP 706 makes vulnerable fallback unreachable
# - setuptools upgraded to >=78.1.1 (CVE-2025-47273)
# - HTTPS-only package downloads enforced
# - No --trusted-host flags used
# - Non-root execution limits filesystem access
#
# Review Date: 2026-02-25
# Expiry: 2026-05-25
CVE-2025-8869

# =============================================================================
# CVE-2025-7709: SQLite FTS5 integer overflow
# =============================================================================
# Severity: Medium
# Component: libsqlite3-0
# Description: Integer overflow in FTS5 extension
#
# Risk Assessment:
# - CVSS Score: 5.5 (Medium)
# - Attack Vector: Local
# - Privileges Required: Low
# - User Interaction: None
#
# Justification for Acceptance:
# 1. Mercury Agent does not use SQLite FTS5 (Full-Text Search) extension
# 2. Application uses numpy/pandas for data storage, not SQLite
# 3. SQLite is only present as a transitive dependency
# 4. No user-controlled SQL queries are executed
# 5. Container runs as non-root limiting exploitation impact
#
# Mitigations Applied:
# - System packages updated to latest available versions
# - Non-root container execution
# - No direct SQLite FTS5 usage in application code
#
# Review Date: 2026-01-06
# Expiry: 2026-04-06
CVE-2025-7709

# =============================================================================
# CVE-2025-68973: GnuPG information disclosure and arbitrary code execution
# =============================================================================
# Severity: High
# Component: gpgv
# Description: Information disclosure and potential arbitrary code execution
#              via out-of-bounds write in GnuPG
# Status: No fix available in Debian bookworm
#
# Risk Assessment:
# - CVSS Score: 7.5 (High)
# - Attack Vector: Network
# - Privileges Required: None
# - User Interaction: Required
#
# Justification for Acceptance:
# 1. Mercury Agent does not use GPG for any cryptographic operations
# 2. gpgv is only present as a transitive dependency for apt verification
# 3. Container does not perform package installations at runtime
# 4. Application uses Python cryptography library for all crypto operations
# 5. No user-controlled data is processed by gpgv
#
# Mitigations Applied:
# - Non-root container execution (USER mercuryagent)
# - No runtime package installations
# - Application uses modern cryptography library (not GPG)
# - Multi-stage build minimizes attack surface
#
# Review Date: 2026-01-06
# Expiry: 2026-04-06 (re-evaluate when Debian patch available)
CVE-2025-68973

