# =============================================================================
# CVE-2023-45853: zlib heap-based buffer overflow (Critical)
# =============================================================================
# Severity: Critical
# Component: zlib1g
# Description: Integer overflow and resultant heap-based buffer overflow
#              in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6
# Status: will_not_fix (Debian has marked this as won't fix)
#
# Risk Assessment:
# - CVSS Score: 9.8 (Critical)
# - Attack Vector: Network
# - Privileges Required: None
# - User Interaction: None
#
# Justification for Acceptance:
# 1. Vulnerability is in minizip contrib code, not core zlib
# 2. Mercury Agent does not use minizip or zip file creation
# 3. Application uses Python zipfile module (not affected)
# 4. Debian has marked this as "will_not_fix" for bookworm
# 5. The vulnerable function (zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6) is not called
#
# Mitigations Applied:
# - Non-root container execution
# - No minizip usage in application code
# - Python zipfile module used for any archive operations
# - System packages updated to latest available versions
#
# Review Date: 2026-01-06
# Expiry: 2026-04-06 (Debian will_not_fix - monitor for policy change)
CVE-2023-45853

